# Module 4 — Functional Re-annotation, GenBank Reconstruction & Comparison

Galaxy wrapper for functional re-annotation analysis, GenBank reconstruction, secondary metabolite identification, and comparative genome analysis.

## Components

- Galaxy XML wrapper
- Snakemake workflow
- Functional annotation (eggNOG-mapper)
- GenBank reconstruction
- Secondary metabolite analysis (antiSMASH)
- Functional comparison
- Hypothetical protein analysis

## Input

- Protein FASTA files (.faa)
- GenBank files (.gb)
- Prodigal outputs (.fna, .gff, .proteins.faa)
- Replicon metadata (.tsv)
- Annotation databases:
  - go-basic.obo
  - kegg_pathway_titles.tsv
  - pfam_duf_map.tsv

## Output

- Functional annotation summary tables
- Comparative functional analysis tables and figures
- Reconstructed GenBank files
- Secondary metabolite (antiSMASH) tables and figures
- Hypothetical protein comparison tables and figures
- Files prepared for downstream nr-NCBI analysis

## Scope and excluded components

The current Galaxy implementation focuses on the all-CDS analysis workflow, including hypothetical proteins.

The following components were not included:

1. CDS-only analysis
   - Excluded because it overlaps with the all-CDS workflow and may introduce redundant/conflicting interpretation results.
   - The workflow follows the all-CDS strategy to ensure comprehensive CDS analysis, including hypothetical proteins.

2. NCBI NR-based annotation
   - Excluded from the Galaxy implementation due to high computational requirements and complexity.
